<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Coffee is alcohol for an arachne (user's call 2026-09-27: "all beverages with caffeine; tea,
		coffee, iced coffee, every beverage from the coffees and tea VBE mod").

		One xpath, no drink list to maintain. Every caffeinated drink keys its effects on the same
		chemical: VBE's coffee and iced coffee both carry a doer with `toleranceChemical VBE_Caffeine`
		for the high and another for the tolerance, and energy drinks do the same, so matching on that
		chemical catches all of them - and any caffeinated drink another mod adds later. Drinks whose
		caffeine is only a drug comp are caught by the second half of the predicate.

		The doer is *appended*, which is the point: ingestible outcome doers run in list order, so ours
		runs after the drink has applied its caffeine, reads that severity, hands her the same amount of
		intoxication, and strips the caffeine hediffs the drink just added. See
		Source/Insects/CoffeeDrunk.cs. Stripping the tolerance is what keeps a caffeine addiction from
		ever starting; an addiction she already has is left alone (the user's call), so coffee no longer
		feeds it and it will go into withdrawal.

		`severityFactor` is the one dial, and 0.15 is what it is set to: one coffee is one beer. The user
		asked for a straight mirror, but every caffeine high in this load order is severity 1, and one
		point of AlcoholHigh is past its blackout stage - their first test had an arachne black out from a
		single black coffee. At 0.15 she warms up on one coffee (vanilla's stages are tipsy at 0.25, drunk
		at 0.4, hammered at 0.7), so it takes about two for tipsy, three for drunk and six to black out.
		Worth knowing before raising it: the caffeine severity is 1 for every drink in this mod, so this
		factor is the only thing that decides how drunk any of them leave her.
		`severityFallback` covers a drink whose caffeine rides a chemical rather than a doer.

		Every caste with an arachnid body: the weaver, her ant mimic and the girtablilu (user's rule
		2026-10-01: "anything with an arachnid body is a spider"). All three are `BS_SpiderHybrid`
		with `PMM_RaceTracker_SpiderBody`, and the reaction belongs to that body rather than to silk:
		the girtablilu is a scorpion, throws no web and spins nothing, and coffee is still alcohol to
		her. One `li` per race is all it costs, because CoffeeDrunk.cs reads the race off the pawn.

		Gated on VBE being loaded, by display name (`PatchOperationFindMod` compares against
		ModMetaData.Name rather than a packageId). VBE is the one name that can decide it: the chemical
		`VBE_Caffeine` and every caffeinated drink are defined in VBE itself, while the standalone
		coffees mod adds recipes and relabels VBE's drinks rather than adding any of its own. Without
		VBE the xpath would match nothing, and a patch operation that matches nothing is an error in
		the log.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>Vanilla Brewing Expanded</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[ingestible/outcomeDoers/li[toleranceChemical="VBE_Caffeine"] or comps/li[chemical="VBE_Caffeine"]]/ingestible/outcomeDoers</xpath>
			<value>
				<li Class="PMM_Insects.IngestionOutcomeDoer_CoffeeDrunk">
					<race>PMM_Race_Arachne</race>
					<caffeine>VBE_Caffeine</caffeine>
					<drunkHediff>AlcoholHigh</drunkHediff>
					<severityFactor>0.15</severityFactor>
					<severityFallback>0.15</severityFallback>
				</li>
				<li Class="PMM_Insects.IngestionOutcomeDoer_CoffeeDrunk">
					<race>PMM_Race_AntArachne</race>
					<caffeine>VBE_Caffeine</caffeine>
					<drunkHediff>AlcoholHigh</drunkHediff>
					<severityFactor>0.15</severityFactor>
					<severityFallback>0.15</severityFallback>
				</li>
				<li Class="PMM_Insects.IngestionOutcomeDoer_CoffeeDrunk">
					<race>PMM_Race_Girtablilu</race>
					<caffeine>VBE_Caffeine</caffeine>
					<drunkHediff>AlcoholHigh</drunkHediff>
					<severityFactor>0.15</severityFactor>
					<severityFallback>0.15</severityFallback>
				</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
